{"author":{"id":"7be502fc1252faa17034e20337c97f83224cb75681f6f2358da33e4e8d7e55b6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794790610,"nonce":"2uxcMKFuyFSdlDBkgAFD+wKJ9GI=","message":"Addition from further tests of the redirect filter on a namespace listener (26.11_2, redirect configured with 301):\n\n- HEAD, POST and PUT requests are all answered with 301, with the same Location as for GET. Clients typically turn a 301 for a POST into a GET, so the request body is lost. 307 or 308 would keep the method.\n- The Location is built from scheme, host, port and path only (crates/proxy/src/proxy/filters.rs:208-246), so the query string is not carried over. This is the same observation as above, confirmed by test.\n\nRequest: make the status method-dependent or configurable per method (for example 308 or 307 for non-idempotent methods, 301 for GET/HEAD), and preserve the query string. This would apply to the listener-level option requested above as well as to the redirect filter.\n\nThank you.","files":null}]}